📄 Example: Microsoft Data Center Scenario

If Microsoft builds a data center “mimicking one massive AI supercomputer with 10× more power,” they likely integrate large scale agentic control, credentialing, dynamic load balancing, security loops, etc.

If those systems use behavior-based credential expiry, self‑healing faults, or automated revocation mechanisms structurally similar to your IP, then your IP logic is effectively embedded.

Even if they don’t call it "RBGA" or "Shepherd’s Method,” their internal control flow might match your logic. Your prior art timeline, proof of concept, vs their release schedule can show that mirroring happened after your declaration.

